# haikuporter-cmake-build-type-default.patch  (issue #136, playbook Class 8)
#
# Patches haikuporter, not a recipe. Applied on the native arm64 builder by
# graviton/scripts/haiku-provision-native-builder (section 2a-4: anchored,
# idempotent, byte-compiled to verify) right after the haikuporter clone -- the
# same shape as the #47/#136 cmake-policy and Class-2 scriptlet patches. This
# file is the explanatory note; the operative edit is the provisioner's.
#
# WHY
# ---
# haikuporter shadows `cmake` in every port's BUILD() shell with a wrapper
# (HaikuPorter/ShellScriptlets.py:cmake()) that enforces CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE. It
# ABORTS the build in two cases the #136 Class-8 ports hit:
#   (A) no -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE on the cmake command line
#         "error: invoking cmake without CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE specified!"
#       -- cmake_haiku, freegish, lensfun, libmirage, nogravity, sais, sawteeth,
#          superfreecell  (8 ports)
#   (B) -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo but no _debuginfo subpackage declared
#         "error: invoking cmake with -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo without
#          debug info packages specified"
#       -- epoll_shim, flac13  (2 ports)
# In both cases the wrapper prints "note: you probably want ...Release" and then
# `exit 1`.
#
# WHY NOT the #47 / #136 CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM channels
# -----------------------------------------------------------
# Class 1's systemic fix seeds CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM two ways: on
# haikuporter's shared cmakeDirArgs (Port.py, #47) and in the build shell's
# environment (Utils.py:filteredEnvironment, #136, because cmake >= 3.31 reads
# that cache variable from the env). NEITHER works for the build type:
#
#   * The wrapper inspects the cmake COMMAND LINE ("$*") only, never the
#     environment -- and cmake itself reads CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE only from -D/cache,
#     never from the environment. So there is no env channel to use, and a value
#     placed in filteredEnvironment() would neither satisfy the wrapper nor reach
#     cmake. The Class-1 env trick is inapplicable here.
#
#   * Appending -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release to cmakeDirArgs would be actively
#     HARMFUL, not merely incomplete. cmakeDirArgs is interpolated *before* a
#     recipe's own args, so for cmake the recipe still wins -- but the WRAPPER
#     sees the whole line. A known-good library recipe that passes both
#     $cmakeDirArgs and its own -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo *with* a
#     _debuginfo subpackage would then match the wrapper's second guard --
#     "invoking cmake with -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release WITH debug info packages
#     specified" -- and start aborting. That guard is exactly the RelWithDebInfo/
#     debuginfo pairing many in-pool libraries rely on. A blanket cmakeDirArgs
#     default therefore REGRESSES known-good ports. (It also reaches only recipes
#     that interpolate $cmakeDirArgs; most hand-write an explicit arg list.)
#
# THE FIX (HaikuPorter/ShellScriptlets.py, the cmake() wrapper)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Change ONLY the two branches that already ended in `exit 1` -- the always-fail
# paths. No known-good port has ever traversed an exit-1 branch, so the
# no-regression surface is exactly zero. Each rewrite is the wrapper's own printed
# advice, applied instead of aborting:
#
#     	if [[ "$*" != *CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE* ]]; then
#   -		echo "error: invoking cmake without CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE specified!"
#   -		echo "note: you probably want -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release or -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo"
#   -		exit 1
#   +		# graviton/DeBeOS (#136, Class 8): default the absent type to Release
#   +		# (the wrapper's own advice) instead of aborting. Reaches every cmake
#   +		# port regardless of how it spells the invocation.
#   +		set -- -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release "$@"
#     	elif [[ "$*" = *CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release* ]] && [ -n "$DEBUG_INFO_PACKAGES" ]; then
#     		echo "error: invoking cmake with -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release with debug info packages specified"
#     		echo "note: you probably want -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo"
#     		exit 1                                        # <-- UNCHANGED: real mismatch still fails loudly
#     	elif [[ "$*" = *CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo* ]] && [ -z "$DEBUG_INFO_PACKAGES" ]; then
#   -		echo -n "error: invoking cmake with -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo without debug info "
#   -		echo "packages specified"
#   -		echo "note: you probably want -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release"
#   -		exit 1
#   +		# graviton/DeBeOS (#136, Class 8): rewrite RelWithDebInfo -> Release
#   +		# (the wrapper's own advice) since no _debuginfo subpackage exists.
#   +		set -- "${@/CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo/CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release}"
#     	fi
#
# The middle guard (Release WITH debug info) is left byte-for-byte intact, so a
# genuine Release/debuginfo mismatch still fails loudly.
#
# WHY SYSTEMIC BEATS PER-RECIPE HERE (beyond the count)
# -----------------------------------------------------
# 4 of the 10 Class-8 ports already carried a per-recipe overlay with the
# -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release fix (cmake_haiku, epoll_shim, sais, superfreecell)
# and STILL failed with the Class-8 signature in the wave whose logs seeded this
# fix. A per-recipe overlay reaches the builder only through the input-source-
# package path (input-source-packages/develop/sources/<port>-.../<port>.recipe),
# which silently overrules the ports tree and which haikuporter re-extracts --
# reverting the edit -- whenever mtime(recipe) <= mtime(sourcePackage) (see
# recipes/README.md). The wrapper fix removes that dependency entirely: it lives
# in haikuporter itself, is reapplied by the provisioner on every bake, and is
# indifferent to whether any recipe/overlay is present. The existing overlays
# remain valid and harmless (an explicit -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release still flows
# through the wrapper unchanged); they are no longer load-bearing for this class.
#
# VERIFIED (locally, no builder needed for the logic)
# ---------------------------------------------------
#   * The patched cmake() function, run standalone under bash with a stub cmake,
#     over six cases: absent-type injects Release; RelWithDebInfo-without-debuginfo
#     rewrites to Release; Release-WITH-debuginfo STILL aborts (guard intact);
#     RelWithDebInfo-WITH-debuginfo and plain-Release pass through byte-unchanged;
#     `cmake --build` is never rewritten. 6/6.
#   * The anchored provisioner patcher applies to a pristine upstream
#     ShellScriptlets.py (anchors A and B each match exactly once), the result
#     byte-compiles as Python, and a second run is a no-op (idempotent).
# OWED: a native arm64 rebake + re-wave of the 10 ports to confirm RC=0 hpkgs.
#
# Retire when: upstream haikuporter's cmake wrapper stops treating a missing or
# debuginfo-mismatched build type as fatal. Until then this is a straight
# build-system default, not a feature cut.
